  "composer": {
    "accepted_prose": "Tomi leaned back in her chair, tapping a finger against her chin as she considered the question. She let the silence stretch just long enough to make it clear she was thinking, not hesitating. Finally, she shrugged.\n\n\"Okay, so if you're talking strictly timing—like, when I head out or come back—I guess I wouldn't mind knowing if someone's around. But here's the thing: I don't need you or anyone else analyzing my schedule. If it's just 'Tomi left at three,' that's whatever. But the second it becomes 'Tomi's been gone a while,' we have a problem. Curiosity's fine; just don't make it your business to report on me.\"\n\nShe flashed a quick grin, casual but with an edge. \"So yeah, limited data. And I'm the one who decides what's useful. Got it?\"\n\nAfter Tomi finished, Aoi smiled warmly and turned her attention to the question directed at her. Her voice was soft and practical.\n\n\"For the hallway or back door, a quick message five minutes before you come or go would be perfect. That way we can avoid any awkward surprises. Nothing strict—just a heads-up so I can make sure I'm not in your way or leaving something in the hall.\"\n\nShe clasped her hands lightly in front of her, the picture of reasonable cooperation. \"That should cover the shared spaces. The rest can stay flexible.\"",
